From: Robert DeLanghe <1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 15:16:23 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] fix(opencode): mint projected ids in opencode's own shape
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

OpenCode Zen's free tier rejects any request whose x-opencode-session
header is not an opencode-shaped id (`ses_` + 12 hex + 14 base62) with
403 FreeTierError "can only be used from within OpenCode". Projected
sessions carried `ses_` + 24 hex, so every `path resume --harness
opencode` session was refused while native sessions answered.
Established by replaying captured requests: the projected body passes
unchanged once the header has the right shape; the time field is not
checked for recency.

Session, message and part ids now go through one minter that writes
opencode's format — 12 hex of the low 48 bits of time*4096+counter
(inverted for sessions) plus 14 base62 chars from the SHA-1 of the old
seed — so projections stay deterministic and, as a side effect, part
ids are monotonic within a message the way opencode orders them.
`ses_`-prefixed view ids are still kept verbatim.

Verified: codex -> opencode headless with opencode/big-pickle replies
(rc 0, no error event); `path goldens check` 46 ok.
